.TH LIBMPQ__WRITER_BEGIN 3 2026-08-18 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__writer_begin \- begin an MPQ streaming file writer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__writer_begin("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s *" "mpq_archive,"
.BI "        const char *" "filename,"
.BI "        libmpq__off_t " "unpacked_size,"
.BI "        const mpq_file_options_s *" "options,"
.BI "        mpq_writer_s **" "writer"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Begins \fIfilename\fP with declared \fIunpacked_size\fP and returns an
active, caller-owned \fI*writer\fP. NULL \fIoptions\fP selects writer
defaults. Supply bytes with libmpq__writer_write(3), then call
libmpq__writer_finish(3). Only one writer may be active per archive.
.PP
Add LIBMPQ_FILE_FLAG_SECTOR_CRC to options.flags to generate sector Adler-32
checksums for sectorized COMPRESS or IMPLODE files. Checksums cover packed
bytes before encryption. The checksum table follows the data and is not
encrypted; it uses zlib compression only when smaller than raw storage.
The flag is ignored for empty, raw, and single-unit files. Generation is
opt-in and does not enable implicit verification during extraction.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fBLIBMPQ_SUCCESS\fP with an active writer on success, or a
negative libmpq error. No file entry is published before finish succeeds.
.SH ERRORS
Invalid writer state or storage options return \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT\fP;
duplicate names return \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST\fP; invalid sizes or exhausted
capacity return \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_SIZE\fP. Allocation and I/O errors may
also propagate.
